    "summary": "A video circulating on social media shows residents in Somalia's Southwest state burning the Turkish flag, reflecting growing public anger over reported Turkish airstrikes that have killed civilians and livestock.",
    "content": "A video circulating on social media this week shows a group of Somali residents in the country's Southwest state setting fire to the Turkish flag while holding up their own regional banner. The act is a visible sign of mounting frustration toward Turkey, a nation long considered one of Somalia's most dependable partners.\n\nIn the footage, men and women accuse Turkey of bombing rural communities, killing livestock, and allegedly harming children. These grievances, they say, have become unbearable, leading to the public display of defiance. The video has sparked widespread discussion online, with many Somalis expressing sympathy for the protesters' sentiments.\n\nThe incident occurs against a backdrop of increasing Turkish military involvement in Somalia, particularly airstrikes targeting areas believed to be hideouts for militant groups. However, reports of civilian casualties have fueled resentment among local populations, who feel caught in the crossfire.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development is significant as it signals a shift in perception of a key international ally. Many diaspora members have previously supported Turkish investments and aid projects in Somalia, but this event may prompt a reevaluation of Ankara's role and underscore the importance of accountability in foreign military operations.\n\nThe Somali government has yet to issue an official response to the video. Turkey has not commented on the specific allegations, but has previously stated its operations are aimed at stabilizing the region. As tensions simmer, observers call for dialogue to address the concerns of affected communities.\n\nRead the original report from Somalia Guardian here: https://www.somaliguardian.com/news/somalia-news/somalis-burn-turkish-flag-ankara-airstrikes-resentment/",
