    "content": "Authorities in Puntland, a semi-autonomous region in northeastern Somalia, announced the arrest of several young people in the port city of Bossaso. The suspects are accused of using the social media platform TikTok to advertise and sell alcohol, which is prohibited in the region. The arrests were carried out by the Bari Regional Police Command as part of a broader crackdown on illegal activities.\n\nThe operation underscores the growing challenge of online platforms being used for unlawful commerce. In recent years, social media has become a common tool for various businesses in Somalia, but authorities have been working to ensure that these platforms are not misused for activities that violate local laws and cultural norms. Alcohol sale and consumption are strictly regulated in Puntland, and offenders face legal consequences.\n\nThe suspects, whose identities have not been disclosed, are currently in police custody and will be referred to the judicial system for further processing. Local officials have urged the public to report any illegal activities, including online sales of prohibited substances, to assist law enforcement in maintaining order.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this news highlights the importance of understanding and respecting the legal frameworks in their homeland. Many diaspora members engage in business ventures in Somalia, and this case serves as a reminder that online activities are subject to local laws. It also demonstrates the vigilance of Puntland authorities in adapting to new technological trends while upholding regional regulations.\n\nThe community in Bossaso has expressed mixed reactions, with some supporting the police action as necessary for social harmony, while others call for more educational campaigns to prevent youth from engaging in such activities. The police have reaffirmed their commitment to continuing such operations to deter similar offenses in the future.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/booliska-puntland-oo-qabtay-dhalinyaro-khamri-ku-iibinaysay-aaladda-tiktok/424858/",
